# A SHELL SCRIPT WITH CRLF LINE ENDINGS DIES ON macOS.
#
# The error is `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`, and it would appear for the first
# time inside an Xcode Cloud build log, on a machine nobody here can open,
# against a file that is correct in every other respect — right directory,
# right name, executable bit set, contents exactly as intended.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf on, so the working copy
# is CRLF and the blob happens to be LF. HAPPENS TO BE is the problem: it is a
# property of one git setting on one machine rather than of the repository.
# This makes it a fact about the repository instead.
#
# Same family as the CRLF entry in CLAUDE.md, where three "anchor not found"
# failures in a row were blamed on indentation and quoting before anyone
# printed the bytes.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Xcode project files are line-ending sensitive in the same way and are
# generated on macOS. Keep them LF so a Windows checkout cannot rewrite them.
*.pbxproj text eol=lf
*.xcconfig text eol=lf
*.swift text eol=lf
